The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
if (arena.isRunning()) {
    if (lockFoodLevel) {
        event.setCancelled(true);
    }
}
```
Reason:
The absence of a check to verify if the player is actually in the arena means that when the food level lock is enabled, the food level change event is cancelled for all players on the server, not just those within the arena. This leads to unintended gameplay consequences for players outside the arena.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
if (arena.inArena(p) && lockFoodLevel) {
    event.setCancelled(true);
}
```
Reason:
By adding the condition `arena.inArena(p)`, the code now ensures that the food level change event is only cancelled for players who are actually in the arena when the food level lock is enabled. This restricts the effect of the food level lock to only those players within the arena, resolving the unintended impact on other players.

